# WS6-05 (handle release on drop, no double close after an explicit close). Sources:
# spec/03-ownership.md (an owned handle drops exactly once at scope end through its
# `freedBy` deleter; a `take` call moves it, so the scope end does not drop it again)
# and the dos/exec/utility/timer autodocs (each acquire has one matching release).
# Expected: "9 2" (every acquire succeeded) and, under `--vamos-leaks`, no orphan
# memory, no library left open, and no vamos error (a second release of a lock or a
# FreeMem of a freed block fails the run).
# Detector: the vamos leak detector fired on the seeded program (WS5 red check); the
# contrast changes the count after the explicit timer free (output discriminates);
# the release check itself rests on the detector.
profiles: hosted-amiga
expect: output
contrast: count = count + 1;\n    }\n    let l: Lock? ==> count = count + 2;\n    }\n    let l: Lock?
contrast-expect: output
--- output
9 2
--- contrast-output
9 3
